# The sidebar switch's runtime state. It records the user's own on/off choice,
# so it belongs to a deployment, never to the repository — and a committed copy
# would silently disable the guard (and, worse, disable it inside the test suite,
# which asserts the ENABLED behaviour).
.peak-guard-state.json
.peak-guard-state.json.boot.json

# Diagnostics and scratch left behind while developing the plugin.
.probe*
.pg-probe*
*.tmp

# The plugin-authoring research notes. They were gathered while building this
# plugin and quote this machine's absolute paths (the harness home, credential
# and profile locations), so they stay local. The conclusions that matter to a
# user are already folded into README.md / README.zh.md.
DSH-PLUGIN-AUTHORING-REPORT.md

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
